==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/teɪk‿ˈɪn/|a=RP,GA,CA}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-take in.wav|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/tæɪk‿ˈɪn/|a=AU}}
* {{IPA|en|/tæɪk‿ˈən/|a=NZ}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|<,,took,taken>}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[receive]].
#: {{hypo|en|rake in}}
#: {{ux|en|The company '''took in''' more than forty million euros last year.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[receive]] and properly [[absorb]] or [[comprehend]].
#: {{ux|en|The news is a lot to '''take in''' right now.}}
#: {{ux|en|I was so sleepy that I hardly '''took in''' any of the lecture.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[enjoy]] or [[appreciate]].
#: {{ux|en|I'm just going to sit on a bench and '''take in''' the scenery.}}
#: {{ux|en|Just relax and '''take in''' the fresh ocean air.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[allow]] a [[person]] or an [[animal]] to [[live]] in one's [[home]].
#: {{ux|en|'''take in''' a stray cat}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[receive]] (goods) into one's home for the purpose of [[process]]ing for a [[fee]].
#: {{ux|en|In hard times, some women would '''take in''' washing and others dressmaking repairs.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To shorten (a garment) or make it smaller.
#: {{ant|en|let out|let down}}
#: {{ux|en|Try '''taking''' the skirt '''in''' a little around the waist.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[attend]] a [[showing]] of.
#: {{ux|en|'''take in''' a show}}
#: {{ux|en|'''take in''' a movie}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1986|title=Long Time Passing: Lives Of Older Lesbians|editor=Marcy Adelman|chapter=Always Me|author=Rusty Brown|page=149|text={{...}} and for lack of anything else to do I thought I'd '''take in''' a strip show.}}
# {{senseid|en|deceive}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[deceive]]; to [[hoodwink]].
#: {{ux|en|Their grandma lost thousands of dollars because she was '''taken in''' by scammers.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|climbing}} To tighten (a belaying rope).
#: {{syn|en|take up}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[subscribe]] to [[home]] [[delivery]] of.
#* '''1844''' January 23, cross-examination in the case of ''R v Daniel O'Connell, et al.'', reprinted in, 1844, John Flanedy, editor, ''A Special Report of the Proceedings in the Case of the Queen against Daniel O'Connell{{...}} on an Indictment for Conspiracy and Misdemeanour'', page 218&nbsp;[http://google.com/books?id=do7RAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA218&dq=%22take+in+no+newspaper%22]:
# {{lb|en|nautical}} To [[reef]].
#* {{RQ:Dana Two Years|chapter=[[s:Two Years Before the Mast/Chapter XXXV|Chapter XXXV]]|passage=The second mate holds on to the main top-gallant sail until a heavy sea is shipped, and washes over the forecastle as though the whole ocean had come aboard; when a noise further aft shows that that sail, too, is '''taking in'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[arrest]] (a person).
#: {{syn|en|take up}}
#: {{ux|en|The police '''took in''' the suspect.}}

